abstract: >-
  A Hadamard matrix of order 4792 = 8 * 599, an order listed as open in the
  2026 survey of Egan, Kotsireas, London and O Cathain. Miyamoto's theorem
  gives order 8m from a conference matrix of order m+1 and a quaternary
  Hadamard matrix of order m-1; the quaternary input may be replaced by a
  real Hadamard matrix of order 2(m-1) whose rows and columns pair into 2x2
  Hadamard blocks, allowing reflections as well as rotations. A paired-block
  matrix of order 1196 comes from the Cooper-Wallis array of order 52 with
  Williamson-type matrices of order 23, two of them equal, obtained from a
  self-complementary regular two-graph on 46 vertices. The software rebuilds
  the matrix and checks every pair of distinct rows.
